          </span>
          <span>View on GitHub</span>
          <span class="github-button__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">Open source · Runs alongside your Discord bot</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-visual">
      <img src="/assets/panel.png" alt="EasySupport ticket panel in Discord, showing support categories members can choose from">
      <figcaption>One panel. A clear way to ask for help.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section class="workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
    <div class="workflow-copy">
      <p class="section-kicker">Built around the conversation</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-heading">From request to resolution.</h2>
      <p>
        Give every request a private place, keep staff on the same page, and leave a useful record when the work is done.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="<%= repoUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the source on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="workflow-visual">
      <img src="/assets/ticket.png" alt="An EasySupport ticket showing its status controls, intake answers, and conversation">
      <figcaption>Staff actions and ticket context stay together.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
    <div class="capabilities-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">The essentials, connected</p>
      <h2 id="capabilities-heading">Stay on top of support.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-list">
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Tickets in one click</h3>
        <p>Publish a panel with a button for each category. Members answer intake questions before a private channel is created.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Staff workflows</h3>
        <p>Claim, update, escalate, and close tickets using configurable status controls. Every action is recorded in your log channel.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Useful endings</h3>
        <p>Save TXT and HTML transcripts when tickets close, then invite members to rate the support they received.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability">
        <h3>Your server, your data</h3>
        <p>Run the bot and website together on your own server with a shared MySQL database and a single configuration flow.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing-callout" aria-labelledby="closing-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">Open source and self-hosted</p>
      <h2 id="closing-heading">Better support, simply.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="github-button github-button--light" href="<%= repoUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      <span class="github-button__icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 496 512" focusable="false">
